Build a production-quality frontend UI for a decentralized exchange called "SHREE SWAP".

This is a Uniswap-inspired Ethereum Sepolia testnet DEX for a custom ERC-20 token.

Token:
- Name: SHREE
- Symbol: SH
- Maximum supply: 1,000,000 SH
- Initial circulating supply: 500,000 SH
- Trading pair: SH / ETH
- Network: Ethereum Sepolia
- Wallet: MetaMask

IMPORTANT:
This is a blockchain application UI. Do not create fake backend data or pretend transactions are real. The frontend should be structured so that real smart-contract integration can be connected later through ethers.js.

DESIGN:
Create a clean, simple, elegant fintech-style interface.
Avoid gaming aesthetics.
Avoid excessive gradients.
Avoid excessive cards.
Use a light background with navy/indigo text and subtle cyan/blue accents.
Use generous spacing, rounded corners, subtle borders and minimal shadows.
Make the interface responsive for desktop and mobile.

HEADER:
- SHREE SWAP logo/text
- Navigation: Swap, Liquidity, Transactions
- Network indicator: Ethereum Sepolia
- Connect Wallet button
- When connected, show shortened wallet address

MAIN SWAP PAGE:

Create a centered swap card.

Title:
"Swap SH ↔ ETH"

Subtitle:
"Trade SHREE tokens on Ethereum Sepolia"

Swap input:
Label: "You pay"
Large amount input
Token selector: SH
Show available SH balance

Swap direction button between the two inputs.

Second input:
Label: "You receive"
Large amount input/output
Token selector: ETH
Show available ETH balance

Below inputs display:
- Exchange rate
- Minimum received
- Price impact
- Liquidity provider fee
- Route: SH → ETH

Primary button:
"Connect Wallet" when disconnected
"Enter amount" when no amount entered
"Approve SH" for SH → ETH before approval
"Swap" when ready

LIQUIDITY PAGE:

Title:
"SH / ETH Liquidity Pool"

Display:
- SH reserve
- ETH reserve
- Current price
- Total liquidity

Create an elegant Add Liquidity section:

SH amount input
ETH amount input

Display:
- Pool share
- Current price
- Deposit amounts

Buttons:
"Approve SH"
"Add Liquidity"

Also include a Remove Liquidity section.

TRANSACTIONS PAGE:

Title:
"Recent Swaps"

Create a clean table/list containing:
- Time
- Wallet
- Direction
- SH amount
- ETH amount
- Transaction status
- View transaction

Each transaction should have a link placeholder for Ethereum Sepolia block explorer.

POOL OVERVIEW:

On the Swap page, below the swap card, show a compact SH/ETH pool overview:
- SH reserve
- ETH reserve
- Current price
- 24h volume placeholder
- Liquidity

Do not use fake numerical blockchain statistics. If no smart-contract data is available, show "--" or "Connect wallet".

TECHNICAL STRUCTURE:

Use:
- Next.js/React
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui components
- lucide-react icons

Create reusable components:
- Header
- WalletButton
- TokenInput
- SwapCard
- PoolStats
- LiquidityCard
- TransactionList
- TransactionStatus
- NetworkBadge

Keep blockchain integration isolated in a services/hooks layer so ethers.js contract integration can be added later.

Create placeholder contract configuration:
- SHREE token contract address
- SHREE Swap contract address
- Ethereum Sepolia chain ID

Do not implement a centralized backend for swaps.

The visual result should look like a professional small DEX rather than a generic crypto dashboard.